        ":question/problem": "What are the dimensions of $CD$, if $C$ is a $2\\times 9$ matrix and $D$ is a $9\\times 8$ matrix?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "There are $9$ columns in $C$ and $9$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $C$ equals the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication, and $CD$ is a $2\\times 8$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{C}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{9}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{D}_{\\boxed{\\text{9}}\\times 8}={CD}_{2\\times 8}\n$$",
